<% provide(:title, "Notification Retention") %>

<div class="container-fluid py-4" id="notification-retention-dashboard">
  <div class="d-flex flex-wrap justify-content-between align-items-center gap-3 mb-4">
    <div>
      <h1 class="h3 mb-1"><i class="bi bi-archive me-2"></i>Notification Retention Assessment</h1>
      <p class="text-muted mb-0">Administrator-only, read-only review of notification and delivery-attempt record ages.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="d-flex gap-2">
      <%= link_to "Operations Dashboard", infrastructure_notification_operations_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary" %>
      <%= link_to "Refresh", infrastructure_notification_retention_path, class: "btn btn-outline-primary" %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="alert alert-info" role="status">
    <strong>Assessment only.</strong> No deletion, archival, or changes to notification records are performed.
    The <%= @assessment[:retention_days] %>-day period is a configurable planning assumption, not an approved retention policy.
  </div>

  <div class="card shadow-sm mb-4">
    <div class="card-body d-flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <div><strong>Assessment time:</strong> <%= @assessment[:assessed_at].utc.strftime("%d %b %Y %H:%M UTC") %></div>
      <div><strong>Older than:</strong> <%= @assessment[:cutoff_at].utc.strftime("%d %b %Y %H:%M UTC") %></div>
      <div><span class="badge bg-secondary">Read-only</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="h5 mb-3">Retention overview</h2>
  <div class="row g-3 mb-4" id="notification-retention-kpis">
    <% [
      ["Total notifications", @assessment[:total_notifications], "primary"],
      ["Accepted notifications", @assessment[:accepted_notifications], "success"],
      ["Aged accepted candidates", @assessment[:candidate_notifications], "warning"],
      ["Candidates with audit attempts", @assessment[:candidate_with_attempts], "info"],
      ["Protected notifications", @assessment[:protected_notifications], "secondary"],
      ["Total delivery attempts", @assessment[:total_attempts], "primary"],
      ["Aged delivery attempts", @assessment[:aged_attempts], "warning"]
    ].each do |label, value, colour| %>
      <div class="col-sm-6 col-xl-4">
        <div class="card shadow-sm h-100"><div class="card-body">
          <div class="small text-muted"><%= label %></div>
          <div class="h3 mt-2 mb-0 text-<%= colour %>"><%= number_with_delimiter(value) %></div>
        </div></div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="row g-3 mb-4">
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="card shadow-sm h-100" id="notification-retention-protected">
        <div class="card-header fw-semibold">Protected operational statuses</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="small text-muted">These records are excluded from the candidate assessment regardless of age.</p>
          <dl class="row mb-0">
            <% %w[Pending Sending Unknown].each do |status| %>
              <dt class="col-8"><%= status %></dt>
              <dd class="col-4 text-end"><%= number_with_delimiter(@assessment[:protected_by_status].fetch(status, 0)) %></dd>
            <% end %>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="card shadow-sm h-100" id="notification-retention-controls">
        <div class="card-header fw-semibold">Audit safeguards</div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <p>Delivery attempts remain linked to their parent notifications. Candidate counts do not authorise deletion.</p>
          <p class="mb-0">Before introducing any cleanup, approve a retention schedule, legal-hold process, investigation protections, archival approach and recovery procedure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="alert alert-light border small" role="note">
    <strong>Interpretation:</strong> “Aged accepted candidates” means Accepted notifications created before the cutoff.
    “Aged delivery attempts” is an independent count based on attempted_at; it does not imply those attempts can be deleted.
    Accepted indicates Microsoft Graph accepted submission, not confirmed recipient delivery.
  </div>
</div>
